(4747794, 682685, 86447, '<td valign="top">I think the reason this didn''t score as well as it could have is almost exclusively the crop.  The chin and forehead don''t bother me as much as the lack of space to the left.     <br/> <br/>But, you''re right.  She''s beautiful.</td>', 'I think the reason this didn''t score as well as it could have is almost exclusively the crop.  The chin and forehead don''t bother me as much as the lack of space to the left.      But, you''re right.  She''s beautiful.', '2008-06-04 10:05:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4747817, 682685, 67697, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful portrait!  So natural and warm.  She has a beautiful smile and this pose you captured is so flattering.  I love that hair!  If you go back to the comments I made in mine, I noted that studio portraits were gonna be the more favored ones.  I know those require a lot of work to, but I like the challenge of spontaneous shooting.  I think this is what you have here and you did a wonderful job!</td>', 'This is a wonderful portrait!  So natural and warm.  She has a beautiful smile and this pose you captured is so flattering.  I love that hair!  If you go back to the comments I made in mine, I noted that studio portraits were gonna be the more favored ones.  I know those require a lot of work to, but I like the challenge of spontaneous shooting.  I think this is what you have here and you did a wonderful job!', '2008-06-04 10:14:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(4747928, 682766, 70689, '<td valign="top">Nice composition and viewpoint. I like the way you used nudity in a very natural fashion, and I think you were right in choosing this one instead of the outtake. I do think you could have scored higher if you gave this one the same PP though. I think the pic is a bit too dark, whereas the brightness of your outtake jumps right onto the viewer.<br/> <br/>And I have to admit I am a sucker for frickles and redheads. :)</td>', 'Nice composition and viewpoint. I like the way you used nudity in a very natural fashion, and I think you were right in choosing this one instead of the outtake. I do think you could have scored higher if you gave this one the same PP though. I think the pic is a bit too dark, whereas the brightness of your outtake jumps right onto the viewer. And I have to admit I am a sucker for frickles and redheads. :)', '2008-06-04 10:31:04.000000', NULL, 0),
