(4755584, 682460, 34462, '<td valign="top">Wonderful textures, wonderful contrast and softness, wonderful portrait. You were robbed... This should have scored much higher.</td>', 'Wonderful textures, wonderful contrast and softness, wonderful portrait. You were robbed... This should have scored much higher.', '2008-06-07 09:40:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(4755837, 682687, 77196, '<td valign="top">No expert, but I think a couple of things may have caused the sub-5 votes. First, the washout in the upper right 1/4 of the shot. Second, the shot lacks the ultra-crispness of focus on subject. Third, the feeling of distance from the subject - I feel like I''m looking at the scene, and not drawn into it. I didn''t vote on your shot, but for me, it is very nice. I love the balance between the washout and wall - almost symmetrical. Very nice leading lines that wind up focusing your attention on her face.</td>', 'No expert, but I think a couple of things may have caused the sub-5 votes. First, the washout in the upper right 1/4 of the shot. Second, the shot lacks the ultra-crispness of focus on subject. Third, the feeling of distance from the subject - I feel like I''m looking at the scene, and not drawn into it. I didn''t vote on your shot, but for me, it is very nice. I love the balance between the washout and wall - almost symmetrical. Very nice leading lines that wind up focusing your attention on her face.', '2008-06-07 12:34:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(4755850, 682919, 77196, '<td valign="top">Absolutely love the expression - to me almost an amused tolerance with a mischievous glint. There is also a feeling of quiet admiration - she is pleased with the person she''s looking at. This shot draws me in. Excellent job of exposure, getting the detail in the shadow under the hat without blowing out the cheeks.</td>', 'Absolutely love the expression - to me almost an amused tolerance with a mischievous glint. There is also a feeling of quiet admiration - she is pleased with the person she''s looking at. This shot draws me in. Excellent job of exposure, getting the detail in the shadow under the hat without blowing out the cheeks.', '2008-06-07 12:41:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4755866, 682688, 77196, '<td valign="top">Love this shot. Not only is she adorable, but those eyes are compelling! Her expression is interesting - not quite clear what it is - makes you wonder what''s going on in her head. The blush in her cheeks match the pink of her collar. I could easily see this in a 4'' square on a museum wall.</td>', 'Love this shot. Not only is she adorable, but those eyes are compelling! Her expression is interesting - not quite clear what it is - makes you wonder what''s going on in her head. The blush in her cheeks match the pink of her collar. I could easily see this in a 4'' square on a museum wall.', '2008-06-07 12:48:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4755875, 682725, 77196, '<td valign="top">Tell Lolo there is no way she looks anywhere near 70 in the picture. You''ve done a wonderful, captivating job of capturing her kind soul. I can easily see her inviting neighborhood children in for warm cookies and a glass of milk. In this shot, it feels to me like she''s just sat down and is ready to listen. I love the happy lines on her face. They speak of a good life with lots of pleasant memories.</td>', 'Tell Lolo there is no way she looks anywhere near 70 in the picture. You''ve done a wonderful, captivating job of capturing her kind soul. I can easily see her inviting neighborhood children in for warm cookies and a glass of milk. In this shot, it feels to me like she''s just sat down and is ready to listen. I love the happy lines on her face. They speak of a good life with lots of pleasant memories.', '2008-06-07 12:53:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4755896, 681577, 77196, '<td valign="top">Without the tons of sub-4 scores, this would have been a high-scoring shot (and well deservedly so). Different is not always well received here, but don''t let that stop you. It is refreshing, after 60 head shots of lovely ladies, to encounter something different. If this is an example of your work, we''re all in trouble. Welcome to dpchallenge! Looking forward to seeing more of your work.</td>', 'Without the tons of sub-4 scores, this would have been a high-scoring shot (and well deservedly so). Different is not always well received here, but don''t let that stop you. It is refreshing, after 60 head shots of lovely ladies, to encounter something different. If this is an example of your work, we''re all in trouble. Welcome to dpchallenge! Looking forward to seeing more of your work.', '2008-06-07 13:05:58.000000', NULL, 0),
