(4844651, 682790, 63269, '<td valign="top">This is so, so powerful and moving. For me personally, this is an image that I will remember much more than most of the other photos of studio-lit smiley girls in this challenge. Not that there''s anything wrong with those photos, it''s just that this one has so much more to it. Superb work.</td>', 'This is so, so powerful and moving. For me personally, this is an image that I will remember much more than most of the other photos of studio-lit smiley girls in this challenge. Not that there''s anything wrong with those photos, it''s just that this one has so much more to it. Superb work.', '2008-07-25 14:40:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(4845293, 682218, 32345, '<td valign="top">Great portrait, very underrated.</td>', 'Great portrait, very underrated.', '2008-07-26 00:54:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(4846075, 682218, 88204, '<td valign="top">I thought I should circle back with you. I mentioned you in the comments of one of my images <a href="//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=684701" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=684701</a> because I was inspired by your photo. I love the intimacy of your shot... I''m fascinated how the camera allows the viewer to be so close to the subject without having ever met. To be this close would be SUCH an invasion of personal space, yet the photo makes it okay. Interesting in a weird way.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I wasn''t trying to duplicate your shot but I wanted something that had a similar intimacy. I think I pushed the wide angle distortion a little more than you. My daughter did the modeling for me because she''s much more pleasing to look at up close than me.  :)<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks for the great image and thanks for the inspiration. I wanted to make sure you know your work is appreciated and has spawned creativity in others (or copycats).<br/> <br/>Thanks!<br/>Chris<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-07-26 23:06:07.</i></td>', 'I thought I should circle back with you. I mentioned you in the comments of one of my images //dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=684701 because I was inspired by your photo. I love the intimacy of your shot... I''m fascinated how the camera allows the viewer to be so close to the subject without having ever met. To be this close would be SUCH an invasion of personal space, yet the photo makes it okay. Interesting in a weird way. Anyway, I wasn''t trying to duplicate your shot but I wanted something that had a similar intimacy. I think I pushed the wide angle distortion a little more than you. My daughter did the modeling for me because she''s much more pleasing to look at up close than me.  :) Anyway, thanks for the great image and thanks for the inspiration. I wanted to make sure you know your work is appreciated and has spawned creativity in others (or copycats). Thanks!Chris', '2008-07-27 00:05:21.000000', '2008-07-27 00:06:07.000000', 0),
